# Cloudflare Pages direct-upload asset exclusions.
#
# `wrangler pages deploy` uploads pages_build_output_dir ("." for this project)
# as publicly-fetchable static assets. It only auto-excludes node_modules,
# .DS_Store, and .git — it does NOT consult .gitignore. Everything listed here
# would otherwise be uploaded and made fetchable by anyone as a static file.
#
# This does NOT affect Pages Functions: `functions/api/*.js` importing from
# `lib/*.js` is resolved and bundled into the Worker at BUILD time by
# Wrangler's function bundler (esbuild), which reads source files from disk
# directly — it is a separate step from the static-asset upload this file
# governs. Excluding lib/ here only stops it from being served as a
# downloadable URL; it does not stop Functions from importing it.
#
# Secrets — never let local dev secrets reach a public asset URL.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.example

# Server-side/source-only code — not meant to be fetchable, and lib/ imports
# are inlined into the Functions Worker bundle at build time regardless.
lib/
test/
migrations/

# Project docs and planning artifacts — not part of the public site.
docs/
.superpowers/
*.md

# Tooling/config — irrelevant (and potentially informative to an attacker)
# as a public asset.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
wrangler.toml
vitest.config.js
.gitignore
.npmrc
